# W3 pins. Synthetic append-only corpus, generated by scripts/bench/gen-w3.py.
# Reproduce: ./scripts/bench/gen-w3.py --build $DIR 1   (and 2)
# Check before measuring: ./scripts/bench/gen-w3.py --verify $DIR 1   (and 2)
# SYNTHETIC and labelled synthetic: the mechanism is the exhibit —
# appends preserve alignment, so fixed blocks work fine. No download needed;
# the generator is seeded xorshift64, pure ASCII, and reads no clock.
# Pin = gen-w3.py --digest DIR: sha256 over a domain tag and then, in
# corpus.rs's own walk order (per-directory memcmp sort, depth first),
# one length-prefixed record per node carrying exactly the fields
# crates/granary-bench/src/corpus.rs records — lstat type, the exec bit, the
# length and sha256 of file content, symlink target bytes, empty-directory
# markers — and finally the node count. A file type corpus.rs refuses (fifo,
# socket, device) makes --digest refuse too, rather than skipping it.
# Shape, so a reader can tell a real tree from an empty or half-written one:
#   v1  24 files    103,680,000 bytes   svc-{00..23}.log @ 4,320,000
#   v2  26 files    143,424,000 bytes   svc-* @ 5,616,000,
#                                       late-{00,01}.log @ 4,320,000
# Every file in both versions is >= 4x MIN_GRAIN (512 KiB, thresh.rs:23) AND
# >= 2x the sweep grid's coarsest min (1 MiB = the 2 MiB grid point's avg/2),
# so none of them is single-grain at any point on the grid. gen-w3.py asserts
# both bounds at import; crates/granary-bench/tests/gen_w3_constants.rs
# asserts its copies of the two Rust constants against their sources.
# v1 is a strict byte prefix of v2 in all 24 svc-* files: 103,680,000 bytes
# unchanged, 31,104,000 appended (1,296,000 per file), and 8,640,000 more in
# the 2 files that exist only in v2.
# Verified on 2026-08-11 (python 3.14.2, macOS 26.5.2, aarch64): three
# builds at three different paths produced the v1 digest below and `diff -r`
# reported the trees identical. The walker that compares lstat type, mode
# bits, symlink targets, empty directories and full content is the --digest
# above, and its coverage is a COMMITTED check, not a transient run:
# `gen-w3.py --self-test` builds tiny v1/v2 trees and asserts the append-only
# property for all 24 files, that late-* exists only in v2, and that the
# digest moves for a one-byte in-place flip, a one-byte append, an exec bit,
# an added empty directory, a dangling symlink, a changed symlink target, a
# symlink to a directory, and a file replaced by a symlink to identical
# content — plus every guard's named refusal. 41 cases.
v1 7b9ebe5f97fa0e1f3200a0c50071ae5a99d98974d49d5e7294fa3afef9b03d8b
v2 cb6d994bd0568f74c249ffb770f99cf9f7ecc13c7e9d269250ad87add527fe2c
